## Analysis
### What is the association between your two classes? Dependency 
### What multiplicity did you choose and why? Many-to-many 
### How did you implement the relationship in Python? By referring to a player as one whole
### Why did you store an object reference instead of copying its data? To make it simpler 
### If your relationship uses many, why is a list appropriate? So it can store more information and be counted as one.
